<span id="A7.T13.9.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.T13.9.2.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">where do polar bears live and what’s their habitat</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A7.T13.9.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">
<span id="A7.T13.9.2.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="A7.T13.9.2.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.T13.9.2.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">Puzzle bears are a type of bear that live in the Arctic regions, specifically in the Arctic tundra. These bears are known for their thick fur, which helps them survive the cold climate. They are also known for their ability to hibernate during the long winter months. The Arctic tundra is a cold, treeless region that surrounds the North Pole. It is characterized by low temperatures, strong winds, and permafrost. Puzzle bears are well-adapted to this environment, with a thick layer of fat and fur that helps them stay warm. […]</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A7.T13.9.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">
<span id="A7.T13.9.2.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="A7.T13.9.2.3.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.T13.9.2.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">show set the stage for the next phase of the war, which was the Battle of the Somme, in 1916. The Battle of the Somme was a major battle in World War I, and it was one of the bloodiest battles of the war, with over 1 million casualties on both sides. The battle was a failure for the Allies, as they were unable to achieve their objectives and the German army was able to push back the French and British forces. The battle is often considered a turning point in the war, as it marked the beginning of the war’s stalemate and the shift towards trench warfare. […]</span></span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A7.T13.9.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A7.T13.9.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t">
<span id="A7.T13.9.3.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:99.6pt;">
<span id="A7.T13.9.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.T13.9.3.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">what is artificial intelligence</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A7.T13.9.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">
<span id="A7.T13.9.3.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="A7.T13.9.3.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.T13.9.3.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">****Artificial Intelligence (AI)** is a branch of computer science that focuses on creating machines or software capable of performing tasks that typically require human intelligence. These tasks include learning, reasoning, problem-solving, perception, and language understanding. ### Key Concepts in AI: </span>
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A7.T13.9.3.2.1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">1. **Machine Learning (ML)**: A subset of AI where systems learn from data without being explicitly programmed. Examples include:
- **Supervised Learning**: The model learns from labeled data (e.g., classification, regression).
- **Unsupervised Learning**: The model finds patterns in unlabeled data (e.g., clustering, dimensionality reduction).
- **Reinforcement Learning**: The model learns by interacting with an environment and receiving feedback (e.g., game-playing agents). […]</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A7.T13.9.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">
<span id="A7.T13.9.3.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="A7.T13.9.3.3.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.T13.9.3.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">1. The problem statement, all variables and given/known data </span>
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A7.T13.9.3.3.1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">A 1.00 kg block is placed on a frictionless horizontal surface. A 100 N force is applied to the block at an angle of 30 degrees above the horizontal. What is the acceleration of the block?
</span>
