<tr id="A7.T13.9.4" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A7.T13.9.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t">
<span id="A7.T13.9.4.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:99.6pt;">
<span id="A7.T13.9.4.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.T13.9.4.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">The 2000 British film Snatch was later adapted into a television series for what streaming service?</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A7.T13.9.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t">
<span id="A7.T13.9.4.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="A7.T13.9.4.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.T13.9.4.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">The “Sweeney Todd” series is a British television series that aired on BBC One. It is a miniseries adaptation of the musical “Sweeney Todd: The Demon Barber of Fleet Street” by Stephen Sondheim. The series was first broadcast in 2007 and is known for its dark, gothic tone and faithful adaptation of the original musical.</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A7.T13.9.4.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t">
<span id="A7.T13.9.4.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="A7.T13.9.4.3.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.T13.9.4.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">Okay, so I need to figure out the answer to this question: “What is the name of the famous mathematician who was also a philosopher and a writer, known for his work on the foundations of mathematics and logic, and who is often associated with the development of set theory and the concept of the continuum¿‘ Hmm, let me think.
First, the question mentions a mathematician who was also a philosopher and a writer. That narrows it down. I remember that there are several mathematicians who were also philosophers, like Kurt Gödel, Bertrand Russell, and maybe someone else. But the question specifically mentions set theory and the continuum. […]</span></span>
</span></td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</figure>
